{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PCuAaABv9cd6nuTCjB2Xtu","type":"tool_result","content":"57:15. `npx size-limit` on `dist/`:\n58:    - core 4.17 kB (limit 4.2 kB)\n59:    - `microtags/htm` 1.43 kB (limit 5 kB)\n60:    - `microtags/htm` browser 4.56 kB (limit 4.6 kB)\n61:    - baseline `origin/main` core: 3.48 kB (limit 3.5 kB)\n65:## Bundle sizes\n67:Measured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\n72:| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n73:| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n77:Stripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\n82:imports, so comparing the 23 kB client to the 26 kB server is not like\n271:Core grew from 3.48 kB to 4.17 kB brotli (+20%), and the size limit was\n272:raised from 3.5 kB to 4.2 kB. The browser templater is at 4.56 kB against\n273:a 4.6 kB limit. Net effect in this example: 23.88 kB to 23.11 kB.\n278:Measure again with all renders stripped.\n345:handling (`factory.ts:118-122`). A setup that calls a method on a nested\n378:   (finding 8).\n379:3. ADR-005 line 64 says \"The core size budget stays at 3.5 kB\".\n380:   `.size-limit.js` now allows 4.2 kB, and the measured size is 4.17 kB.\n383:   static render (+0.69 kB brotli).\n407:5. Client bundle smaller: technically met, marginal. 23.11 kB stripped\n408:   against 23.88 kB unstripped (-3.2% minified, -1.6% gzip). Server-render\n409:   code stays in core regardless of stripping (finding 8).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"871ab629-50f7-4bcf-b98c-3172e797b7d3","uuid":"c4fd2088-5add-4ddb-ab65-bf7d2fb0ddf5","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:59:04.837Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"57:15. `npx size-limit` on `dist/`:\n58:    - core 4.17 kB (limit 4.2 kB)\n59:    - `microtags/htm` 1.43 kB (limit 5 kB)\n60:    - `microtags/htm` browser 4.56 kB (limit 4.6 kB)\n61:    - baseline `origin/main` core: 3.48 kB (limit 3.5 kB)\n65:## Bundle sizes\n67:Measured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\n72:| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n73:| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n77:Stripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\n82:imports, so comparing the 23 kB client to the 26 kB server is not like\n271:Core grew from 3.48 kB to 4.17 kB brotli (+20%), and the size limit was\n272:raised from 3.5 kB to 4.2 kB. The browser templater is at 4.56 kB against\n273:a 4.6 kB limit. Net effect in this example: 23.88 kB to 23.11 kB.\n278:Measure again with all renders stripped.\n345:handling (`factory.ts:118-122`). A setup that calls a method on a nested\n378:   (finding 8).\n379:3. ADR-005 line 64 says \"The core size budget stays at 3.5 kB\".\n380:   `.size-limit.js` now allows 4.2 kB, and the measured size is 4.17 kB.\n383:   static render (+0.69 kB brotli).\n407:5. Client bundle smaller: technically met, marginal. 23.11 kB stripped\n408:   against 23.88 kB unstripped (-3.2% minified, -1.6% gzip). Server-render\n409:   code stays in core regardless of stripping (finding 8).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PCuAaABv9cd6nuTCjB2Xtu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pu3pQWdAmDjaYPvk7GNuHU","type":"tool_result","content":"_public/\nAGENTS.md\nCHANGELOG.md\nCONTEXT.md\ndocs/\neslint.config.js\nexample/\nexample-hydration/\nlib.es5.d.ts\nLICENSE\nnode_modules/\npackage.json\nplaywright.config.ts\nREADME.md\nscripts/\nsrc/\ntest/\ntsconfig.build.json\ntsconfig.json\ntsconfig.typecheck.json\nvite.config.ts\n.scratch:\nhydration-dx-fixes/\nmillitags-lessons/\nunidirectional-hydration/\n\n.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes:\nissues/\nprogress.md\nspec.md\n\n.scratch/millitags-lessons:\nissues/\nprogress.md\nspec.md\n\n.scratch/unidirectional-hydration:\nissues/\nlogs/\nprogress.md\nreview-2026-10-13-hydration-dx.md\nspec.md\n\ndocs/adr:\nADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md\nADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md\nADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md\nADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\nADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\nADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\nADR-007-client-templater.md\nADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\nINDEX.md\n\nsrc:\nattributes.ts\nbuild.ts\nbuilders.ts\ncli.ts\ncontext.ts\nesbuild.ts\nfactory.ts\nhtm.browser.ts\nhtm.ts\nindex.ts\nreactivity.ts\nrender.ts\nsetup-context.ts\ntypes.ts\nutil.ts\nvite.ts\n# Architecture Decision Records\n\nDecisions that are hard to reverse, surprising without context, and the\nresult of a real trade-off. See `docs/agents/domain.md` for how agents\nconsume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n\n| # | Decision | Date |\n|---|----------|------|\n| [ADR-001](ADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md) | alien-signals as the reactivity primitive | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-002](ADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md) | No Shadow DOM | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-003](ADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md) | Standard Schema for prop validation | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-004](ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md) | Client bundle size outranks API ergonomics | 2026-07-25 |\n| [ADR-005](ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md) | Single-file components with build-time stripping of render code | 2026-09-23 |\n| [ADR-006][adr-006] | Authored HTML scaffold served by Hono | 2026-09-25 |\n| [ADR-007][adr-007] | Client templater: signal props, reactive regions, mount | 2026-10-04 |\n| [ADR-008][adr-008] | Serialized server state and unidirectional hydration | 2026-10-04 |\n\n[adr-006]: ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\n[adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\n[adr-008]: ADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\n{\n  \"name\": \"microtags\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.14\",\n  \"description\": \"Web component helper\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/index.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./min\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.min.js\"\n    },\n    \"./render\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/render.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/render.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/render.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./context\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/context.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/context.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/context.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./util\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/util.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/util.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/util.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./build\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/build.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/build.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/build.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./esbuild\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/esbuild.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/esbuild.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/esbuild.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./vite\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/vite.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/vite.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/vite.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./htm\": {\n      \"browser\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/htm.browser.d.ts\",\n        \"import\": \"./dist/htm.browser.js\"\n