{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H27o9qr54YvqPRdis8J7Bb","type":"tool_result","content":"9. `npm run lint`: exit 0. `example-hydration/build/` did not exist,\n   because the hydration build failed.\n10. `npm run build:hydration`: exit 1. `failed to load config from\n    .../example-hydration/vite.config.ts ... Error: microtags/build\n    requires \"typescript\" as a peer dependency.`\n11. `npm run test:hydration`: exit 1, same error (its first step is\n    `build:hydration`).\n12. `npm run test:hydration-dev`: exit 1, 0/6. First failure is the same\n    peer-dependency error; the rest fail with `Failed to parse URL from\n    undefined/example-hydration/`.\n13. `npx playwright test` (`test:e2e`): exit 1. `Process from\n    config.webServer was not able to start. Exit code: 1`.\n14. In a scratch copy with finding 1 fixed:\n    - `build:hydration`: exit 0.\n    - `test:hydration`: exit 0, 114/114, plus 17/17 for listen.\n    - `test:hydration-dev`: exit 0, 17/17.\n    - `playwright test`: exit 0, 12 passed (Chromium was available).\n15. `npx size-limit` on `dist/`:\n    - core 4.17 kB (limit 4.2 kB)\n    - `microtags/htm` 1.43 kB (limit 5 kB)\n    - `microtags/htm` browser 4.56 kB (limit 4.6 kB)\n    - baseline `origin/main` core: 3.48 kB (limit 3.5 kB)\n16. `npm run ssr:hydration -- /list`: exit 0, with correct-looking\n    output and state script.\n\n## Bundle sizes\n\nMeasured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\nuses a scratch config with the `microtags()` plugin set to `null`.\n\n| Bundle | Minified | gzip | Unminified |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n| Server `app.js` | not minified | 8,236 B | 26,087 B |\n| Server `listen.js` | not minified | n/a | 896 B |\n\nStripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\nThe unminified diff shows only Counter's render body and `raw()` were\nremoved.\n\nServer `app.js` leaves `hono`, `alien-signals` and `htm` as external\nimports, so comparing the 23 kB client to the 26 kB server is not like\nfor like. The strip on/off comparison is the meaningful one.\n\nLargest pieces of the stripped client (unminified bytes per module):\n\n- `src/htm.browser.ts` 10,921\n- alien-signals 9,946\n- `src/builders.ts` 5,597\n- `src/factory.ts` 4,198\n- `htm` 1,794\n- all pages together, about 3,900\n\n## Findings\n\nOrdered most severe first. Each lists the goal it threatens.\n\n### 1. Blocking (DX). The example's Vite config imports the plugin from source\n\n`example-hydration/vite.config.ts:7`:\nclass = reduce-fouce`. `<noscript>` only covers JavaScript being\ndisabled, not a failed load, a CSP block or an exception. This defeats\nSSR as a fallback.\n\nFix: drop the opacity gate (adoption creates nothing, so there is no\nflash to hide), or add a CSS-only animation that reveals the page after\nN seconds without JS.\n\n### 8. Important (goal 5). Stripping barely shrinks the client\n\nThe stripped client still contains `_renderHost`, `_serializerFor`,\n`_sJson`, `_escAttr` and the `staticRender` wrapper from\n`src/builders.ts`, plus `_str` and `_compArgs` from `htm.browser.ts`.\nThese are built inside `define()` and `Markup.toString`, so stripping a\nuser's `.render` can never remove them.\n\nCore grew from 3.48 kB to 4.17 kB brotli (+20%), and the size limit was\nraised from 3.5 kB to 4.2 kB. The browser templater is at 4.56 kB against\na 4.6 kB limit. Net effect in this example: 23.88 kB to 23.11 kB.\n\nFix: move static-render construction out of `define()`. For example,\nhave `.render()` attach the serializer lazily from a separate module, so\nstripping `.render` also drops `_renderHost` and the serializers.\nMeasure again with all renders stripped.\n\n### 9. Minor (goal 3). Mismatch recovery cascades, and the warning is not dev-only\n\nOn a tag mismatch, `_adopt` advances one DOM node (line 486), so one\nextra server node misaligns every later sibling.\n\nProbe: server `<h1><p><button>`, client `<p><button>`. Warnings:\n`expected <p>, found <h1>` then `expected <button>, found <p>`, and the\nbutton is left unbound.\n\n`console.warn` at lines 466 and 482 is unconditional.\n\nimport type { StandardSchemaV1 } from '@standard-schema/spec'\nimport type { Markup } from './htm.js'\nimport type { Markup as BrowserMarkup } from './htm.browser.js'\nimport type {\n    PropDef,\n    PropType,\n    PropertyOnlyProp,\n    SetupContext,\n    Coercer,\n    RefDef,\n    SingleRefDef,\n    MultipleRefDef,\n    RefsMap,\n    ContextToken,\n    ContextsMap,\n} from './types.js'\nimport {\n    coerceNumber,\n    coerceString,\n    coerceBoolean,\n    coerceJson,\n} from './util.js'\nimport { factory } from './factory.js'\nexport type PropKind = 'prop-only' | 'schema' | 'coercer'\n\nexport interface PropMeta {\n    kind:PropKind\n    coercer:Coercer<unknown>\n    serialize:(value:unknown) => string | null\n}\n\nconst _esc:Record<string, string> = {\n    '&': '&amp;',\n    '\"': '&quot;',\n    \"'\": '&#39;',\n    '<': '&lt;',\n    '>': '&gt;',\n}\nfunction _escAttr (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/[&\"'<>]/g, c => _esc[c])\n}\n\nfunction _sNull ():null { return null }\nfunction _sStr (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v == null ? null : String(v)\n}\nfunction _sBool (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v === true ? '' : null\n}\nfunction _sJson (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v == null ? null : JSON.stringify(v)\n}\n\nfunction _serializerFor (\n    c:Coercer<unknown>, k:PropKind\n):(v:unknown) => string | null {\n    if (k === 'prop-only') return _sNull\n    if (k === 'schema') return _sStr\n    if (c === coerceBoolean) return _sBool\n    if (c === coerceJson) return _sJson\n    return _sStr\n}\n\nfunction _renderHost (\n    tag:string, metas:Record<string, PropMeta>,\n    props:Record<string, unknown>,\n    extra:Record<string, string> | undefined,\n    inner:string\n):string {\n    let a = ''\n    for (const [k, m] of Object.entries(metas)) {\n        if (!(k in props)) continue\n        const s = m.serialize(props[k])\n        if (s === null) continue\n        a += s === '' ? ` ${k}` : ` ${k}=\"${_escAttr(s)}\"`\n    }\n    if (extra) {\n        for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(extra)) {\n            a += v === '' ? ` ${k}` : ` ${k}=\"${_escAttr(v)}\"`\n        }\n    }\n    return `<${tag}${a}>${inner}</${tag}>`\n}\n\n/** The DSL object passed to the withProps callback. */\nexport type PropDSL = {\n    number():Coercer<number>\n    string():Coercer<string>\n    boolean():Coercer<boolean>\n    json<T>():Coercer<T | undefined>\n    schema<T>(validator:StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>):StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>\n    prop<T>(initial:T):PropertyOnlyProp<T>\n}\n\nexport const propDSL:PropDSL = {\n    number: () => coerceNumber,\n    string: () => coerceString,\n    boolean: () => coerceBoolean,\n    json: <T>() => coerceJson as Coercer<T | undefined>,\n    schema: <T>(v:StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>) => v,\n    prop: <T>(initial:T):PropertyOnlyProp<T> => (\n        { _microtag: 'prop', initial }\n    ),\n}\n\n/**\n * DSL object passed to the withRefs callback.\n * Call `r.one()` for a single element or `r.all()` for multiple. Pass a\n * CSS selector to query by it, or omit it to match `[data-ref=\"<key>\"]`.\n *\n * Element typing:\n * - `r.one()` defaults to `HTMLElement`.\n * - `r.one<T>()` sets the type and keeps the `[data-ref]` selector.\n * - `r.one('button')` infers the type from the tag AND queries by that\n *   tag, exactly like `document.querySelector('button')`.\n */\nexport type RefsDSL = {\n    one<K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(\n        selector:K\n    ):SingleRefDef<HTMLElementTagNameMap[K]>\n    one<T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(selector?:string):SingleRefDef<T>\n\n    all<K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(\n        selector:K\n    ):MultipleRefDef<HTMLElementTagNameMap[K]>\n    all<T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(selector?:string):MultipleRefDef<T>\n}\n\nexport const refsDSL:RefsDSL = {\n    one: ((selector?:string):SingleRefDef => (\n        { _microtag: 'ref:one', selector }\n    )) as RefsDSL['one'],\n    all: ((selector?:string):MultipleRefDef => (\n        { _microtag: 'ref:all', selector }\n    )) as RefsDSL['all'],\n}\n\n/**\n * DSL object passed to the withContexts callback.\n * Currently a no-op placeholder; the user references imported\n * context tokens directly in the returned record.\n */\nexport type ContextDSL = Record<never, never>\nconst contextDSL:ContextDSL = {}\n\n/**\n * Maps each declared ref key to its own name as a string literal. Exposed\n * as the static `refs` on a registered element so server-rendered templates\n * can fill in `data-ref` values without hardcoding the names, e.g.\n * `data-ref=\"${MyCounter.refs.dec}\"`.\n */\nexport type RefNames<RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef>> = {\n    readonly [K in keyof RefDefs]:K & string\n}\n\n/** Plain values for props (not signals) in the render context. */\nexport type RenderProps<Defs extends Record<string, PropDef>> = {\n    [K in keyof Defs]:PropType<Defs[K]>\n}\n\nexport interface RenderContext<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n    RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef> = Record<never, never>,\n> {\n    props:RenderProps<Props>\n    refs:RefNames<RefDefs>\n    TAG:string\n    children:string\n    attrs:Record<string, string>\n}\n\nexport type RenderFn<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n    RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef> = Record<never, never>,\n> = (\n    ctx:RenderContext<Props, RefDefs>\n) => string | Markup | BrowserMarkup\n\nexport interface RenderOptions {\n    client?:boolean\n}\n\nexport type StaticRenderFn<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef>,\n> = (\n    props:RenderProps<Props>,\n    options?:{ children?:string; attrs?:Record<string, string> }\n) => string\n\n/**\n * A host element: an `HTMLElement` with a property accessor for each\n * declared prop, typed as the prop's value. At runtime a signal may also\n * be assigned (via a cast), making the prop read through to it.\n */\nexport type MicrotagHost<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n> = HTMLElement & RenderProps<Props>\n\n/**\n * A registered custom element class that also exposes, as static members,\n * the tag name it was registered under (`TAG`) and the names of its\n * declared refs (`refs`).\n */\nexport type MicrotagElementClass<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n    RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef> = Record<never, never>,\n> = {\n    new ():MicrotagHost<Props>\n    readonly prototype:MicrotagHost<Props>\n    /** The custom element tag name, e.g. 'my-counter'. */\n    readonly TAG:string\n    /**\n     * The declared ref names, each mapping to its own `data-ref` string.\n     * Lets server-rendered markup reference refs by key instead of a magic\n     * string: `MyCounter.refs.dec`.\n     */\n    readonly refs:RefNames<RefDefs>\n    readonly render:StaticRenderFn<Props>\n    readonly props:readonly (keyof Props & string)[]\n}\n\n/**\n * Fluent builder that accumulates props/refs/contexts config\n * before registering a custom element via `.setup()`.\n */\nexport class ComponentBuilder<\n    Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n    RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef> = Record<never, never>,\n    CtxDefs extends Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>> = Record<never, never>,\n> {\n    private readonly _coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>>\n    private readonly _observed:string[]\n    private readonly _propNames:string[]\n    private readonly _propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta>\n    private readonly _refDefs:Record<string, RefDef>\n    private readonly _ctxDefs:Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>>\n    private readonly _renderFn?:RenderFn<Props, RefDefs>\n\n    constructor (\n        readonly tagName:string,\n        coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>> = {},\n        observed:string[] = [],\n        refDefs:Record<string, RefDef> = {},\n        ctxDefs:Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>> = {},\n        propNames:string[] = [],\n        propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta> = {},\n        renderFn?:RenderFn<any, any>,\n    ) {\n        this._coercers = coercers\n        this._observed = observed\n        this._propNames = propNames\n        this._propMetas = propMetas\n        this._refDefs = refDefs\n        this._ctxDefs = ctxDefs\n        this._renderFn = renderFn as\n            RenderFn<Props, RefDefs> | undefined\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * The custom element tag name, e.g. 'my-counter'. Available at every\n     * point in the fluent chain since each builder method returns a new\n     * builder carrying the same tag name.\n     */\n    get TAG ():string {\n        return this.tagName\n    }\n\n    withProps<P extends Record<string, PropDef>> (\n        fn:(p:PropDSL) => P\n    ):ComponentBuilder<P, RefDefs, CtxDefs> {\n        const defs = fn(propDSL)\n        const coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>> = {}\n        const observed:string[] = []\n        const propNames:string[] = []\n        const propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta> = {}\n\n        for (const [name, def] of Object.entries(defs)) {\n            const coercer = normalizePropDef(\n                name,\n                def as PropDef<unknown>\n            )\n            coercers[name] = coercer\n            propNames.push(name)\n\n            const kind = isPropOnly(def) ?\n                'prop-only' as const :\n                isStandardSchema(def) ?\n                    'schema' as const :\n                    'coercer' as const\n\n            propMetas[name] = {\n                kind,\n                coercer,\n                serialize: _serializerFor(\n                    coercer,\n                    kind\n                ),\n            }\n\n            if (!isPropOnly(def)) {\n                observed.push(name)\n            }\n        }\n\n        return new ComponentBuilder<P, RefDefs, CtxDefs>(\n            this.tagName,\n            coercers,\n            observed,\n            this._refDefs,\n            this._ctxDefs,\n            propNames,\n            propMetas,\n        )\n    }\n\n    withRefs<R extends Record<string, RefDef>> (\n        fn:(r:RefsDSL) => R\n    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs> {\n        const defs = fn(refsDSL)\n        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs>(\n            this.tagName,\n            this._coercers,\n            this._observed,\n            defs,\n            this._ctxDefs,\n            this._propNames,\n            this._propMetas,\n            this._renderFn,\n        )\n    }\n\n    withContexts<C extends Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>>> (\n        fn:(c:ContextDSL) => C\n    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C> {\n        const defs = fn(contextDSL)\n        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C>(\n            this.tagName,\n            this._coercers,\n            this._observed,\n            this._refDefs,\n            defs,\n            this._propNames,\n            this._propMetas,\n            this._renderFn,\n        )\n    }\n\n    render (\n        fn:RenderFn<Props, RefDefs>,\n        _options?:RenderOptions\n    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs> {\n        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs>(\n            this.tagName,\n            this._coercers,\n            this._observed,\n            this._refDefs,\n            this._ctxDefs,\n            this._propNames,\n            this._propMetas,\n            fn,\n        )\n    }\n\n    setup (\n        fn:(ctx:SetupContext<\n            Props,\n            RefsMap<RefDefs>,\n            ContextsMap<CtxDefs>\n        >) => void\n    ):MicrotagElementClass<Props, RefDefs> {\n        const El = factory({\n            props: this._coercers,\n            observedAttrNames: this._observed,\n            refs: this._refDefs,\n            contexts: this._ctxDefs,\n            setup: fn as any,\n        })\n        Object.defineProperty(El, 'TAG', {\n            value: this.tagName,\n            enumerable: true,\n        })\n\n        const refNames:Record<string, string> = {}\n        for (const key of Object.keys(this._refDefs)) {\n            refNames[key] = key\n        }\n        Object.defineProperty(El, 'refs', {\n            value: Object.freeze(refNames),\n            enumerable: true,\n        })\n\n        Object.defineProperty(El, 'props', {\n            value: Object.freeze([...this._propNames]),\n            enumerable: true,\n        })\n\n        if (this._renderFn) {\n            const renderFn = this._renderFn\n            const tagName = this.tagName\n            const propMetas = this._propMetas\n            const frozenRefs = Object.freeze(\n                { ...refNames }\n            ) as RefNames<RefDefs>\n\n            const staticRender:StaticRenderFn<Props> = (\n                props,\n                options\n            ) => {\n                const children = options?.children ?? ''\n                const attrs = options?.attrs ?? {}\n                const innerHTML = renderFn({\n                    props,\n                    refs: frozenRefs,\n                    TAG: tagName,\n                    children,\n                    attrs,\n                })\n                return _renderHost(\n                    tagName,\n                    propMetas,\n                    props as Record<string, unknown>,\n                    Object.keys(attrs).length > 0 ?\n                        attrs :\n                        undefined,\n                    String(innerHTML)\n                )\n            }\n\n            Object.defineProperty(El, 'render', {\n                value: staticRender,\n                enumerable: true,\n            })\n        }\n\n        if (typeof customElements !== 'undefined') {\n            customElements.define(this.tagName, El)\n        }\n        return El as unknown as MicrotagElementClass<Props, RefDefs>\n    }\n}\n\n/** Create a new component builder for the given tag name. */\nexport function define (tagName:string):ComponentBuilder {\n    return new ComponentBuilder(tagName)\n}\n\nfunction isPropOnly (def:unknown):def is PropertyOnlyProp<unknown> {\n    return (\n        typeof def === 'object' &&\n        def !== null &&\n        '_microtag' in def &&\n        (def as { _microtag: unknown })._microtag === 'prop'\n    )\n}\n\nfunction isStandardSchema (def:unknown):def is StandardSchemaV1 {\n    return (\n        typeof def === 'object' &&\n        def !== null &&\n        '~standard' in def\n    )\n}\n\nfunction normalizePropDef (\n    name:string,\n    def:PropDef<unknown>\n):Coercer<unknown> {\n    if (isPropOnly(def)) {\n        return (_raw:string | null) => def.initial\n    }\n    if (isStandardSchema(def)) {\n        const schema = def as StandardSchemaV1\n        return (raw:string | null):unknown => {\n            const result = schema['~standard'].validate(raw)\n            if (result instanceof Promise) {\n                throw new TypeError(\n                    `withProps: async schemas are not supported (prop \"${name}\")`\n                )\n            }\n            if (result.issues) return undefined\n            return result.value\n        }\n    }\n    return def as Coercer<unknown>\n}\nexport { peek, untracked } from './reactivity.js'\nexport { define } from './builders.js'\nexport type { Serialized, Signal, TypedEvent } from './types.js'\nexport type {\n    MicrotagElementClass,\n    MicrotagHost,\n    RenderContext,\n    RenderFn,\n    RenderOptions,\n    RenderProps,\n    StaticRenderFn,\n} from './builders.js'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"871ab629-50f7-4bcf-b98c-3172e797b7d3","uuid":"249073d3-d984-46e3-922a-c3b70ec02392","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:59:07.208Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9. `npm run lint`: exit 0. `example-hydration/build/` did not exist,\n   because the hydration build failed.\n10. `npm run build:hydration`: exit 1. `failed to load config from\n    .../example-hydration/vite.config.ts ... Error: microtags/build\n    requires \"typescript\" as a peer dependency.`\n11. `npm run test:hydration`: exit 1, same error (its first step is\n    `build:hydration`).\n12. `npm run test:hydration-dev`: exit 1, 0/6. First failure is the same\n    peer-dependency error; the rest fail with `Failed to parse URL from\n    undefined/example-hydration/`.\n13. `npx playwright test` (`test:e2e`): exit 1. `Process from\n    config.webServer was not able to start. Exit code: 1`.\n14. In a scratch copy with finding 1 fixed:\n    - `build:hydration`: exit 0.\n    - `test:hydration`: exit 0, 114/114, plus 17/17 for listen.\n    - `test:hydration-dev`: exit 0, 17/17.\n    - `playwright test`: exit 0, 12 passed (Chromium was available).\n15. `npx size-limit` on `dist/`:\n    - core 4.17 kB (limit 4.2 kB)\n    - `microtags/htm` 1.43 kB (limit 5 kB)\n    - `microtags/htm` browser 4.56 kB (limit 4.6 kB)\n    - baseline `origin/main` core: 3.48 kB (limit 3.5 kB)\n16. `npm run ssr:hydration -- /list`: exit 0, with correct-looking\n    output and state script.\n\n## Bundle sizes\n\nMeasured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\nuses a scratch config with the `microtags()` plugin set to `null`.\n\n| Bundle | Minified | gzip | Unminified |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n| Server `app.js` | not minified | 8,236 B | 26,087 B |\n| Server `listen.js` | not minified | n/a | 896 B |\n\nStripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\nThe unminified diff shows only Counter's render body and `raw()` were\nremoved.\n\nServer `app.js` leaves `hono`, `alien-signals` and `htm` as