{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012LCEk9fx63nbcLodeV4NX4","type":"tool_result","content":"# 13: Server-render code reachable only through a render link\n\n**What to build:** The host-tag builder, the prop serializers and\nattribute escaping move out of core into a separate server render\nsupport module, registered by the mechanism ADR-009 chose. Core\nrecords prop metadata (kind and coercer) and the render function, and\ninstalls a minimal `render` static that delegates to the support\nmodule once it has registered. Calling `render` before registration\nthrows an error naming the module to import. The server templater\nregisters the support module, and the browser templater registers it\nwhen it creates a host. Code that calls a component's `render` static\ndirectly imports the support subpath once; the README documents this\nbreaking change.\n\nThe core size budget is lowered to the new measured size rounded up to\nthe next 0.05 kB, recorded in ADR-009. ADR-005's \"core budget stays at\n3.5 kB\" gets a note pointing at ADR-009, and its claim that a browser\nbundle holds hydration code only is amended. ADR-007's claim that core\ngrows \"only by the prop accessors\" is corrected. AGENTS.md's \"Builder\nand serialization\" section is rewritten for the split, and the rule\nfor new coercer types points at the support module.\n\nSource: spec section \"Server-render code out of core's define path\n(finding 8, goal 5)\".\n\n**Blocked by:** 12 (mechanism and numbers), 02 (attribute parity edits\nthe host-rendering path this moves), 05 (children marker emission in\nthe server templater), 07 (Markup brand in both templaters)\n\n**Touches:** `src/builders.ts` (`_renderHost`, `_serializerFor`,\n`_escAttr`, `staticRender`, `withProps` metadata), a new support module\nunder `src/` with a package.json `exports` entry and inclusion in\n`build-cjs`, `build-esm` and `build-esm:min`, `src/htm.ts`,\n`src/htm.browser.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/ssr.ts`, `test/index.ts`,\n`test/types.ts`, `.size-limit.js`, README, AGENTS.md,\n`docs/adr/ADR-005-*.md`, `docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md`,\n`docs/adr/ADR-009-*.md`\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] Calling a component's `render` static with no templater and no\n      support import throws an error that names the support module\n- [ ] After importing the server templater, `render` produces the same\n      host HTML as before, and every existing SSR exact-string\n      assertion passes unchanged\n- [ ] After the browser templater creates a host, `render` works\n      without a separate support import\n- [ ] Core's size-limit entry is lowered to the ADR-009 number and\n      `npm run size` passes\n- [ ] `npm run build`, `npm run test:ssr`, `npm test`,\n      `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run lint` pass\n# 14: Stripping drops the support module from the client\n\n**What to build:** The `microtags/build` transform injects an import\nof the server render support module into any client module where it\nkeeps a render link, so kept components still render in the browser.\nA module where every render link was stripped gets no such import, and\na client bundle with no templater import then contains none of the\nhost-tag, serializer or escaping code. The check is an observable\nbundle property (the support module absent from the bundler's metafile,\nor size against a stripped-and-unused baseline), not minified\nidentifier names.\n\nRepeat the spec's end measurements: core, `microtags/htm`, the browser\ntemplater, the example client with stripping on and off, and the\nall-stripped fixture app. Record the final numbers in ADR-009.\n\nSource: spec section \"Server-render code out of core's define path\n(finding 8, goal 5)\", the transform part.\n\n**Blocked by:** 13\n\n**Touches:** `src/build.ts` (import injection when a render link is\nkept, including under `cascade`), `src/esbuild.ts` and `src/vite.ts`\nonly if they need to forward anything, `test/build.ts`,\n`test/plugins.ts`, new fixtures under `test/fixtures/`,\n`docs/adr/ADR-009-*.md` (final measurements), README\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] Transforming a module with a kept render link adds exactly one\n      support import, and transforming it again adds no second one\n- [ ] Transforming a module where every render link is stripped adds\n      no support import, including after cascade\n- [ ] Bundling an all-stripped fixture with the esbuild plugin yields a\n      metafile with no support module input, and a kept-render fixture\n      yields one with it\n- [ ] The example client still renders Badge and Notice in the browser\n      after a production build\n- [ ] `npm run test:build`, `npm run test:plugins`,\n      `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:e2e` and `npm run size`\n      pass\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a number.\n * Returns NaN if the value cannot be parsed.\n */\nexport function coerceNumber (raw:string | null):number {\n    return raw === null ? NaN : Number(raw)\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a string.\n * Converts null to empty string.\n */\nexport function coerceString (raw:string | null):string {\n    return raw ?? ''\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a boolean.\n * Absence (null) is false; presence of any value (including '') is true.\n */\nexport function coerceBoolean (raw:string | null):boolean {\n    return raw !== null\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a parsed JSON value.\n * Returns undefined if the value is null or cannot be parsed.\n */\nexport function coerceJson<T = unknown> (raw:string | null):T | undefined {\n    if (raw === null) return undefined\n    try {\n        return JSON.parse(raw) as T\n    } catch {\n        return undefined\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * Run every function in the list, ensuring all run even if some throw.\n * After all have run, re-throws the first error encountered.\nimport htm from 'htm'\nimport { effect, effectScope, untracked } from './reactivity.js'\nimport type { MicrotagElementClass } from './builders.js'\nimport type { PropDef } from './types.js'\n\n// Browser build of `microtags/htm`, selected by the `browser` export\n// condition. `html` describes nodes instead of building a string, and\n// `mount` turns that description into DOM with live bindings.\n\nconst _esc:Record<string, string> = {\n    '&': '&amp;',\n    '\"': '&quot;',\n    \"'\": '&#39;',\n    '<': '&lt;',\n    '>': '&gt;',\n}\n\nfunction _escHtml (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/[&\"'<>]/g, c => _esc[c])\n}\n\nconst VOID = new Set([\n    'area', 'base', 'br', 'col', 'embed', 'hr',\n    'img', 'input', 'link', 'meta', 'param',\n    'source', 'track', 'wbr',\n])\n\ntype Comp = MicrotagElementClass<Record<string, PropDef>>\ntype VType = string | Comp | ((...a:unknown[]) => unknown)\n\ninterface VNode {\n    t:VType\n    p:Record<string, unknown> | null\n    c:unknown[]\n}\n\n/**\n * Opaque, trusted output of the templater. In the browser it describes\n * nodes for `mount`; `String(m)` still yields static HTML.\n */\n37:The core entry exports `Signal` and `Serialized<T>` as types.\n45:This is the only runtime change to the core entry.\n92:pay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n112:entry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"871ab629-50f7-4bcf-b98c-3172e797b7d3","uuid":"215309c5-a489-4170-8edb-60bcc05bc074","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:59:38.247Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# 13: Server-render code reachable only through a render link\n\n**What to build:** The host-tag builder, the prop serializers and\nattribute escaping move out of core into a separate server render\nsupport module, registered by the mechanism ADR-009 chose. Core\nrecords prop metadata (kind and coercer) and the render function, and\ninstalls a minimal `render` static that delegates to the support\nmodule once it has registered. Calling `render` before registration\nthrows an error naming the module to import. The server templater\nregisters the support module, and the browser templater registers it\nwhen it creates a host. Code that calls a component's `render` static\ndirectly imports the support subpath once; the README documents this\nbreaking change.\n\nThe core size budget is lowered to the new measured size rounded up to\nthe next 0.05 kB, recorded in ADR-009. ADR-005's \"core budget stays at\n3.5 kB\" gets a note pointing at ADR-009, and its claim that a browser\nbundle holds hydration code only is amended. ADR-007's claim that core\ngrows \"only by the prop accessors\" is corrected. AGENTS.md's \"Builder\nand serialization\" section is rewritten for the split, and the rule\nfor new coercer types points at the support module.\n\nSource: spec section \"Server-render code out of core's define path\n(finding 8, goal 5)\".\n\n**Blocked by:** 12 (mechanism and numbers), 02 (attribute parity edits\nthe host-rendering path this moves), 05 (children marker emission in\nthe server templater), 07 (Markup brand in both templaters)\n\n**Touches:** `src/builders.ts` (`_renderHost`, `_serializerFor`,\n`_escAttr`, `staticRender`, `withProps` metadata), a new support module\nunder `src/` with a package.json `exports` entry and inclusion in\n`build-cjs`, `build-esm` and `build-esm:min`, `src/htm.ts`,\n`src/htm.browser.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/ssr.ts`, `test/index.ts`,\n`test/types.ts`, `.size-limit.js`, README, AGENTS.md,\n`docs/adr/ADR-005-*.md`, `docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md`,\n`docs/adr/ADR-009-*.md`\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] Calling a component's `render` static with no templater and no\n      support import throws an error that names the support module\n- [ ] After importing the server templater, `render` produces the same\n      host HTML as before, and every existing SSR exact-string\n      assertion passes unchanged\n- [ ] After the browser templater creates a host, `render` works\n      without a separate support import\n- [ ] Core's size-limit entry is lowered to the ADR-009 number and\n      `npm run size` passes\n- [ ] `npm run build`, `npm run test:ssr`, `npm test`,\n      `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run lint` pass\n# 14: Stripping drops the support module from the client\n\n**What to build:** The `microtags/build` transform injects an import\nof the server render support module into any client module where it\nkeeps a render link, so kept components still render in the browser.\nA module where every render link was stripped gets no such import, and\na client bundle with no templater import then contains none of the\nhost-tag, serializer or escaping code. The check is an observable\nbundle property (the support module absent from the bundler's metafile,\nor size against a stripped-and-unused baseline), not minified\nidentifier names.\n\nRepeat the spec's end measurements: core, `microtags/htm`, the browser\ntemplater, the example client with stripping on and off, and the\nall-stripped fixture app. Record the final numbers in ADR-009.\n\nSource: spec section \"Server-render code out of core's define path\n(finding 8, goal 5)\", the transform part.\n\n**Blocked by:** 13\n\n**Touches:** `src/build.ts` (import injection when a render link is\nkept, including under `cascade`), `src/esbuild.ts` and `src/vite.ts`\nonly if they need to forward anything, `test/build.ts`,\n`test/plugins.ts`, new fixtures under `test/fixtures/`,\n`docs/adr/ADR-009-*.md` (final measurements), README\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] Transforming a module with a kept render link adds exactly one\n      support import, and transforming it again adds no second one\n- [ ] Transforming a module where every render link is stripped adds\n      no support import, including after cascade\n- [ ] Bundling an all-stripped fixture with the esbuild plugin yields a\n      metafile with no support module input, and a kept-render fixture\n      yields one with it\n- [ ] The example client still renders Badge and Notice in the browser\n      after a production build\n- [ ] `npm run test:build`, `npm run test:plugins`,\n      `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:e2e` and `npm run size`\n      pass\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a number.\n * Returns NaN if the value cannot be parsed.\n */\nexport function coerceNumber (raw:string | null):number {\n    return raw === null ? NaN : Number(raw)\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a string.\n * Converts null to empty string.\n */\nexport function coerceString (raw:string | null):string {\n    return raw ?? ''\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a boolean.\n * Absence (null) is false; presence of any value (including '') is true.\n */\nexport function coerceBoolean (raw:string | null):boolean {\n    return raw !== null\n}\n\n/**\n * Coerce a raw attribute string to a parsed JSON value.\n * Returns undefined if the value is null or cannot be parsed.\n */\nexport function coerceJson<T = unknown> (raw:string | null):T | undefined {\n    if (raw === null) return undefined\n    try {\n        return JSON.parse(raw) as T\n    } catch {\n        return undefined\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * Run every function in the list, ensuring all run even if some throw.\n * After all have run, re-throws the first error encountered.\nimport htm from 'htm'\nimport { effect, effectScope, untracked } from './reactivity.js'\nimport type { MicrotagElementClass } from './builders.js'\nimport type { PropDef } from './types.js'\n\n// Browser build of `microtags/htm`, selected by the `browser` export\n// condition. `html` describes nodes instead of building a string, and\n// `mount` turns that description into DOM with live bindings.\n\nconst _esc:Record<string, string> = {\n    '&': '&amp;',\n    '\"': '&quot;',\n    \"'\": '&#39;',\n    '<': '&lt;',\n    '>': '&gt;',\n}\n\nfunction _escHtml (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/[&\"'<>]/g, c => _esc[c])\n}\n\nconst VOID = new Set([\n    'area', 'base', 'br', 'col', 'embed', 'hr',\n    'img', 'input', 'link', 'meta', 'param',\n    'source', 'track', 'wbr',\n])\n\ntype Comp = MicrotagElementClass<Record<string, PropDef>>\ntype VType = string | Comp | ((...a:unknown[]) => unknown)\n\ninterface VNode {\n    t:VType\n    p:Record<string, unknown> | null\n    c:unknown[]\n}\n\n/**\n * Opaque, trusted output of the templater. In the browser it describes\n * nodes for `mount`; `String(m)` still yields static HTML.\n */\n37:The core entry exports `Signal` and `Serialized<T>` as types.\n45:This is the only runtime change to the core entry.\n92:pay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n112:entry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012LCEk9fx63nbcLodeV4NX4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
