{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DoWAoMkssL5fq2UwWGyJH4","type":"tool_result","content":".scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 38\n.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 176\n.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 406\n# ADR-007: Client templater with signal props, reactive regions, and mount\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe `html` templater in `microtags/htm` runs only on the server. It\nreturns a string, escapes interpolated values, and expands components\nthrough their render links. In the browser there is no way to describe\nthe page, so application state lives in each component's own signals and\npage-level behaviour is manual DOM code: query an element, add a\nlistener, assign `innerHTML`.\n\nAn author coming from React or Preact expects one state object, passed\ndown, changed through named functions, with the DOM following on its\nown. To support that, the same page function must run on both sides: on\nthe server to produce HTML, and in the browser to adopt that HTML and\nkeep it in sync with state.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"871ab629-50f7-4bcf-b98c-3172e797b7d3","uuid":"bbb679d0-0be4-485e-9b76-7784c98782a1","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:02:45.792Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 38\n.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 176\n.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/common/builders.ts: 406\n# ADR-007: Client templater with signal props, reactive regions, and mount\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe `html` templater in `microtags/htm` runs only on the server. It\nreturns a string, escapes interpolated values, and expands components\nthrough their render links. In the browser there is no way to describe\nthe page, so application state lives in each component's own signals and\npage-level behaviour is manual DOM code: query an element, add a\nlistener, assign `innerHTML`.\n\nAn author coming from React or Preact expects one state object, passed\ndown, changed through named functions, with the DOM following on its\nown. To support that, the same page function must run on both sides: on\nthe server to produce HTML, and in the browser to adopt that HTML and\nkeep it in sync with state.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DoWAoMkssL5fq2UwWGyJH4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
