{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MpsbH8gXUatriKWZBR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] ADR-009 exists, is listed in the ADR index, and names one registration mechanism with the reasons the others lost\n[x] ADR-009 records measured sizes for core, the browser templater, and an all-stripped fixture bundle for the chosen mechanism, using the review's method\n[x] ADR-009 states the breaking change for code that calls a component's `render` static without a templater\n[x] `npm run lint` passes and `src/` is unchanged\n\nI chose the **global hook** for how the server render support registers with core. ADR-009 records the decision and the numbers, and is listed in the ADR index as amending ADR-005. `npm run lint` and `npm test` (286/286) pass, `src/` is unchanged, and everything is in one commit (9b36991).\n\n**How the chosen mechanism works.** The support module will be a new subpath, `microtags/render-support`. Importing it sets `globalThis[Symbol.for('microtags.render')]`. A component's `render` static looks the function up there on each call, and throws an error naming the subpath if it's missing.\n\n**Measurements.** I used the review's method (esbuild minified bundle, then size-limit). My baseline matches the review exactly. The fixtures are two components, one with every render link stripped and one with a render link kept:\n\n| | core | browser templater | all-stripped fixture | kept fixture |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline (HEAD) | 4.17 kB | 4.56 kB | 3.83 kB | 3.87 kB |\n| A. Side-effect subpath | 3.90 kB | 4.91 kB | 3.61 kB | 3.98 kB |\n| B. Setter from core | 3.91 kB | 4.92 kB | 3.60 kB | 3.96 kB |\n| C. Global hook (chosen) | 3.93 kB | 4.93 kB | 3.63 kB | 4.00 kB |\n\nIn all three variants, the all-stripped fixture's bundle contains no support module. In a quick inline check, server output was identical to the baseline.\n\n**Why the others lost.** The three are within 0.03 kB of each other, so size didn't decide it. The README documents an import map where each subpath maps to its own self-contained `.min.js` file. With two copies of the package like that:\n1. **A (side-effect subpath)** throws, because the templater registers with a different copy of core. I confirmed this with two copies of `src/`.\n2. **B (setter from core)** only works if the caller registers with the right copy by hand. It would also make the build transform inject three statements instead of one import line.\n3. **C (global hook)** renders correctly.\n\n**Costs the ADR states plainly:**\n- **Breaking change:** code that calls a component's `render` without a templater must import `microtags/render-support` once.\n- **The example doesn't benefit:** it keeps Badge and Notice, so its client still ships the support module.\n- **Keeping a render link costs a bit more:** about +0.13 kB over today, mostly the new error message, which ticket 13 should shorten.\n- **The browser templater goes over budget:** 4.93 kB against its 4.6 kB limit, so its limit will have to rise.\n- **The core budget is provisional:** 3.95 kB, until ticket 13 measures the real change.\n\nI didn't edit ADR-005 itself, because ticket 13 owns its notes. The prototype, fixtures and `measure.sh` are committed under `.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/` for ticket 13 to reuse. I also added a short AGENTS.md section: lint checks `.scratch/` too, and it explains how to run size-limit on variant bundles. Notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":103893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"871ab629-50f7-4bcf-b98c-3172e797b7d3","uuid":"f5de8648-002f-4521-b773-d30a88442cf4","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:04:20.910Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MpsJf3C4t8MjraPtyK"}
